==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|dhrink}} {{qualifier|pronunciation spelling|imitating an Irish accent}}
* {{l|en|drank}} {{qualifier|slang}}
* {{l|en|drinck}}, {{l|en|drinke}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|en|thrink}} {{qualifier|pronunciation spelling}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|drĭngk|a=RP,GA}}, {{IPA|en|/dɹɪŋk/|[d̠ɹ̠˔ʷɪŋk]}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-drink.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋk|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|drinken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|drincan|t=to drink, swallow up, engulf}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*drinkan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*drinkaną|t=to drink}}, of uncertain origin; possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰrenǵ-|t=to draw into one's mouth, sip, gulp}}, nasalised variant of {{m|ine-pro|*dʰreǵ-|t=to draw, glide}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|fy|drinke|t=to drink}}, {{cog|nds|drinken|t=to drink}}, {{cog|nl|drinken|t=to drink}}, {{cog|de|trinken|t=to drink}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|nb|drikke|t=to drink}}, {{cog|nn|drikka|t=to drink}}.
{{col-bottom}}

====Verb====
[[Image:Woman drinking water.jpg|thumb|Woman '''drinking''' a glass of water]]
{{en-verb|drinks|drinking|drank|past2=drunk|past2_qual=southern US|past3=drinked|past3_qual=nonstandard|drunk|past_ptc2=drunken|past_ptc2_qual=chiefly archaic|past_ptc3=drank|past_ptc3_qual=dialectal|past_ptc4=drinked|past_ptc4_qual=all nonstandard, archaic or obsolete|past_ptc5=drinken|past_ptc6=dranken}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[consume]] (a liquid) through the mouth.
#: {{ux|en|He '''drank''' the water I gave him.}}
#: {{ux|en|You can lead a horse to water but you can't make him '''drink'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Shepheardes Calender|chapter=November|folio=47|passage={{...}} There liues ſhee with the bleſſed Gods in bliſſe: / There '''drinks''' the Nectar with Ambroſia mixt {{...}}|year=1586}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Virginians|volume=I|page=283|passage=It was he who proposed the bowl of punch, which was brewed and '''drunk''' in Mrs. Betty’s room, and which Gumbo concocted with exquisite skill.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=2|passage=''That'' the young Mr. Churchills liked—but they did not like him coming round of an evening and '''drinking''' weak whisky-and-water while he held forth on railway debentures and corporation loans. Mr. Barrett, however, by fawning and flattery, seemed to be able to make not only Mrs. Churchill but everyone else do what he desired.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|metonymic}} To [[consume]] the liquid contained within (a bottle, glass, etc.).
#: {{ux|en|Jack '''drank''' the whole bottle by himself.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[consume]] [[alcoholic]] [[beverage]]s.
#: {{ux|en|You've been '''drinking''', haven't you?}}
#: {{ux|en|No thanks, I don't '''drink'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Everyone who is '''drinking''' is drinking, but not everyone who is drinking is '''drinking'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|III|iv|passage=I '''drink''' to the general joy of the whole table, / And to our dear friend Banquo.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Henry Esmond|passage=Bolingbroke always spoke freely when he had '''drunk''' freely.}}
#* {{RQ:Salinger Catcher|page=168|passage=The waiter came up, and I ordered a Coke for her—she didn't '''drink'''—and a Scotch and soda for myself, but the sonuvabitch wouldn't bring me one, so I had a Coke, too.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2007|writer=w:Matthew Weiner|title=w:Mad Men|episode=Smoke Gets in Your Eyes|season=1|number=1|role=w:Roger Sterling|actor=|passage=You don't know how to '''drink'''. Your whole generation, you '''drink''' for the wrong reasons. My generation, we '''drink''' because it's good, because it feels better than unbuttoning your collar, because we deserve it. We '''drink''' because it's what men do.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take in (a liquid), in any manner; to suck up; to absorb; to imbibe.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Georgics|4|passage=Let the purple violets '''drink''' the stream.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take in; to receive within one, through the senses; to inhale; to hear; to see.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|II|ii|passage=My ears have not yet '''drunk''' a hundred words / Of that tongue's utterance.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Works|title=Eloisa to Abelard|Let me {{...}} '''drink''' delicious poison from thy eye.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|passage=to '''drink''' the cooler air}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[toast]] (someone or something) with a drink; to [[drink to]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To smoke, as tobacco.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1630|author={{w|John Taylor (poet)|John Taylor}}|title=A Proclomation or approbation from the King of execration, to euery nation, for Tobaccoes propogration
|passage=And some men now live ninety yeeres and past, / Who never '''dranke''' tobacco first nor last.}}

